1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,620
情報

2
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:02,000
情報

3
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,260
謡 bunu

4
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:09,360
優しい火だまりにチャイムがディレイする

5
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:15,140
方向を撫でる風

6
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,680
息吹は深くなってく

7
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:24,040
遠回りの涙 名前つけた明日

8
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:28,120
重なる未来のノーライン

9
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:58,100
See you next time.

10
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:28,100
See you next time.

11
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:37,760
I don't know why, but people are always apologizing to me.

12
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:42,800
I hear she was born with a strong sixth sense, so she draws spirits over to her.

13
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,680
Her name's even Sadako, like from the rain.

14
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:49,480
Her parents must have had foresight to give her such a perfect name, know what I mean?

15
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:58,500
I'm done. Go ahead.

16
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:07,020
I'm sorry to disappoint you all, but I can't actually see spirits or anything.

17
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,520
Also, my name is Sawako, not Sadako.

18
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:14,960
Sawako, and it's written as Cheerful Child.

19
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:27,460
For some reason, ever since I can remember, everyone has been afraid of me.

20
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:30,520
But all I want is to get along with them.

21
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:33,860
And I'm gonna try my best today, too.

22
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,420
Apparently, there's a ton of famous celebrities that visit there.

23
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:40,520
Hirano, Endo...

24
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:42,260
Hello there.

25
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,580
I think I've got my cheerful greeting down.

26
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:48,860
Morning.

27
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:50,720
Yo, you walked?

28
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:52,760
It's Kazuhaya.

29
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:55,600
Incredible.

30
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:58,520
He's always surrounded by people.

31
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,220
He's cheerful and positive, too.

32
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,080
Hey there, Kuro-Numa.

33
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:03,980
Ryo!

34
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:09,780
He talks to me the same way he talks to everyone else and treats me as Niko.

35
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,160
G-good.

36
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,360
Yo, Ryo.

37
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:14,320
Yo.

38
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:14,860
Ugh.

39
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,280
You do your homework, Kazuhaya?

40
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:20,560
Kazuhaya is the complete opposite of me.

41
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:25,940
It's like everyone gathers around Kazuhaya, and everything just flows from there.

42
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,700
The day of the high school entrance ceremony.

43
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:43,160
Um...

44
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:46,460
If you happen to be looking for Kitahorohai, it's that way.

45
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,020
Thanks a lot.

46
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:57,240
People usually apologize to me when I talk to them.

47
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:00,260
But he smiled and told me thank you.

48
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:07,220
From that day on, Kazehaya has become someone I admire.

49
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:13,220
And one day, I sincerely hope I can become a person like him.

50
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:17,220
Here's the plan. The day before the closing ceremony.

51
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:19,220
Let's do a test of courage.

52
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:21,220
Going?

53
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:25,220
If you plan on going, I'll have this pinned to the bulletin board,

54
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:29,220
so write your name on it. I hope everyone can go.

55
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:32,220
Everyone? But doesn't that mean...

56
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:34,220
You think Sadako's coming?

57
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:37,220
If she does, the real thing might show up.

58
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:40,220
I can't live up to their expectations.

59
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:44,220
If I went and nothing ended up appearing, would it disappoint them?

60
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:48,220
Now, once the closing ceremony ends, it's summer break.

61
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:51,220
And summer break means summer school.

62
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:55,220
So, who wants to come and help their teacher out?

63
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:58,220
I need one person to come before class over break.

64
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:00,220
It's not forever.

65
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:03,220
If nobody volunteers, I'll just choose.

66
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,220
I just want a break.

67
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:07,220
Everyone's stressed out.

68
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:09,220
Um...

69
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:12,220
If you're okay with me, then...

70
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:15,220
Oh, you sure? Thank you, Kuro Numa.

71
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,220
Hey, Teach.

72
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:22,220
Every single time these jobs come up, they fall on Kuro Numa.

73
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:26,220
No way.

74
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:32,220
It just doesn't seem fair to me, dumping all these random duties on her, you know?

75
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:35,220
Then, will you do it, Kazuhaya?

76
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,220
Huh?

77
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:38,220
Hmm...

78
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,220
Y-yeah.

79
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:40,220
I will.

80
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:42,220
He noticed it.

81
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:47,220
That I was doing all these jobs.

82
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:56,220
You must allow me to handle this.

83
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:59,220
It is summer, and I honestly don't have anything to do.

84
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:00,220
I've got time.

85
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:02,220
So much time.

86
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,220
I live nearby and I have so much free time.

87
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:06,220
If that's the case, Kuro Numa it is.

88
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:07,220
That was a close one.

89
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:08,220
What a relief.

90
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:10,220
He noticed it.

91
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:13,220
I thought I was invisible, but he knew.

92
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:18,220
He's such a nice person.

93
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:21,220
That makes me so happy.

94
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:23,220
Sarako!

95
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:25,220
Shina, hi!

96
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:26,220
It's been a while, huh?

97
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,220
It has.

98
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,220
I mean, we're in different classes now.

99
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:30,220
How's yours?

100
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:33,220
Is there anyone from our elementary or middle school?

101
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:35,220
No, but there's this boy.

102
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:37,220
His name is Kazuhaya and he's...

103
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:38,220
Ah!

104
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:39,220
That really cheerful guy?

105
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:41,220
He's not just really cheerful.

106
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:44,220
The guy's 100% cheerful.

107
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:49,220
Actually, it's like his entire existence is made out of pure cheer.

108
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:50,220
Ah!

109
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:51,220
Ah!

110
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,220
Ah!

111
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:53,220
Ah!

112
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,220
Ah!

113
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,220
Ah!

114
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:56,220
Ah!

115
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:57,220
Kazuhaya!

116
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,220
Ah!

117
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,220
Ah!

118
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,220
Oh my gosh!

119
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:01,220
He just heard everything you said!

120
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,220
Say you're sorry!

121
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:03,220
Ah!

122
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:04,220
Say sorry!

123
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:05,220
Ah!

124
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:06,220
Ah!

125
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:07,220
Ah!

126
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:08,220
Ah!

127
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:10,220
My compliment was taken as an insult?

128
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,220
Hey.

129
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,220
Tell me.

130
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:13,220
Just now.

131
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:15,220
What should I take that ass?

132
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:16,220
Ah!

133
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:17,220
Ah!

134
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:18,220
Ah!

135
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:23,220
Ah!

136
00:07:23,220 --> 00:07:24,220
Ah!

137
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:25,220
Ah!

138
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:26,220
Ah...

139
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,220
Ah!

140
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:28,220
Ah!

141
00:07:28,220 --> 00:07:29,220
Okay, roger that.

142
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,220
Ah!

143
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:33,220
Wait a sec, I'm coming over there.

144
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:34,220
Ah!

145
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:37,220
I never really had a chance to talk with you.

146
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:38,220
Ah!

147
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:39,220
Wait...

148
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:42,220
Isn't this amazing, Sadako?

149
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:46,220
Kazuhaya's the type of person that can't sit back and ignore the Outcast in class.

150
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:48,820
Well, my job's done, so see ya!

151
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:55,180
Kaze Haya, he's such a... such a wonderful person.

152
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:58,940
Once I explained my feelings, he understood.

153
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:02,460
He believed me. He didn't call me a liar.

154
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:08,300
I'm glad.

155
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:12,020
Honestly, I totally thought you hated me, Kuro Numa.

156
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,720
Hated? That's not true at all.

157
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:22,440
Actually, I've always wanted to become a cheerful person like you, Kaze Haya. I mean it.

158
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:28,480
Well, I don't know. I'm sure you're overestimating how cheerful a person I am.

159
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:32,460
I'm not, but it's true. Even your name is cheerful.

160
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:34,860
Okay, but what about you?

161
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,280
Sawako.

162
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,960
Sawako Kuro Numa, isn't it?

163
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:48,580
Yeah, but no one really calls me that.

164
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:55,220
I think that this might be the first time I've cleared up a misunderstanding.

165
00:08:55,220 --> 00:09:00,840
Well, when we talked it out, you told me how you really felt.

166
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:07,440
So nice. This person is... so nice.

167
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:12,060
This is... the first time someone calls me by my real name.

168
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:13,340
What a feeling.

169
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:16,200
You should come to the test of courage too, Kuro Numa.

170
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:18,740
The first time in my whole life.

171
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:28,680
I'll do the test of courage, but I'll sign my name in secret.

172
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:30,480
What?

173
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:31,220
Sawako?

174
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:35,640
Yeah, for the test of courage, it'll be way more fun if someone plays the ghost role.

175
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:40,700
And if it's Sawako, just her standing there would make everyone pee their pants.

176
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:43,800
Excuse me.

177
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:46,460
When did you get here?

178
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:51,360
Um, about that role, I'd like to play it if that's alright.

179
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:52,040
Huh?

180
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,600
No, it's fine.

181
00:09:56,980 --> 00:09:58,640
You shouldn't do it unwillingly.

182
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:04,820
Well, when we talked it out, you told me how you really felt.

183
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:11,640
I... haven't done anything unwillingly... ever.

184
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:19,320
I do want to get along better with everyone, but it's not like I'm trying to do it unwillingly for that or anything.

185
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:23,240
If I can do something, it makes me happy to help.

186
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:28,580
But at the same time, I can't live up to everyone's expectations.

187
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,560
I feel bad for saying this, but...

188
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:32,060
What?

189
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:34,120
The real thing won't appear.

190
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:34,620
Huh?

191
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:37,220
I don't have any psychic ability.

192
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,180
You don't?

193
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:39,900
Nope.

194
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:41,340
At all?

195
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:42,280
Yeah.

196
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:48,860
You're just now admitting this?

197
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:51,060
And did you just say everyone's expectations?

198
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,380
You're way off.

199
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:55,720
I can't believe that's what you've been thinking this whole time, right, Chizu?

200
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:58,520
But what the hell are you crying for?

201
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:00,720
I can't take out here she is.

202
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,520
I'm a real selfie for this time.

203
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,920
You're totally off the mark, too.

204
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:08,560
We're counting on you to be our ghost, then, Sarako.

205
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:11,860
Don't worry, we'll keep it a secret between just us.

206
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,700
So scare them to your heart's content.

207
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:16,460
Thank you.

208
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:22,060
I can't believe they understood how I really felt.

209
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:25,940
It may just be a small step, but I feel like I've changed.

210
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:28,580
Thank you so much.

211
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:32,440
I owe it all to you, Kasehaya.

212
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:38,600
A group will head out every ten minutes!

213
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,980
Looks like almost everyone's made it.

214
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:42,700
Sadako's the only one missing.

215
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:43,540
Huh?

216
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:44,640
Well, Sadako...

217
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:46,960
We said we'd keep it a secret!

218
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:48,040
Uh...

219
00:11:48,040 --> 00:12:02,780
I want everyone to have fun, so I'll do my best.

220
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:05,860
So, so dark.

221
00:12:06,140 --> 00:12:07,380
It's kind of spooky.

222
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:07,420
It's kind of spooky.

223
00:12:07,420 --> 00:12:37,400
It's kind of spooky.

224
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:42,320
Those screams are pretty intense.

225
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,280
What do you think is happening in there?

226
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,100
Good job.

227
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,780
I'm so happy.

228
00:12:50,460 --> 00:12:52,880
I managed to help everyone out this much.

229
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,940
Maybe I'll try biting a strand of hair next time.

230
00:12:55,940 --> 00:13:07,540
Kurunuma?

231
00:13:07,540 --> 00:13:08,760
Kasehaya!

232
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:11,380
What are you doing, huh?

233
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:14,440
I was playing the role of the spirit.

234
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,860
Oh, jeez.

235
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:17,840
Could have told me.

236
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:21,080
I did organize this entire thing, after all.

237
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:23,780
I thought you weren't coming.

238
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:30,280
If I did, it would take the chills away from you and wouldn't be as fun.

239
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:31,500
Chills?

240
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,300
What does that mean?

241
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:35,620
You're out here alone.

242
00:13:35,860 --> 00:13:36,540
Aren't you scared?

243
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:40,140
No, I actually kind of like it out here at night.

244
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:42,620
Especially during the summer.

245
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,560
Like the air.

246
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:45,860
The smell.

247
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:48,560
The sound of the leaves.

248
00:13:49,420 --> 00:13:51,080
And the bugs chirping, too.

249
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:55,840
I get it.

250
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,600
It feels kind of nice out here.

251
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,320
So you mind if I chill with you?

252
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,600
But, um, the test of courage.

253
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:06,720
Thanks to someone not showing up,

254
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,680
the number of people ended up odd.

255
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:10,800
So I got left out.

256
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,120
Scary, right?

257
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:19,900
What's happening right now?

258
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:21,780
Sarako!

259
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:24,360
Yano!

260
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:25,660
And Yoshida!

261
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:28,140
Hey, why is Kaze Haya here?

262
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:30,100
If the two of you knew about all this,

263
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:31,160
you should have told me.

264
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:34,520
Being good to her.

265
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,900
I'm cheerful, boys, or something else.

266
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:38,940
I seriously hate you guys.

267
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:40,020
Sarako?

268
00:14:40,820 --> 00:14:41,420
Nice.

269
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:43,700
You were a real spookmaster.

270
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:44,800
Here, drink up.

271
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,260
Wow, thank you.

272
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:55,160
Such great people.

273
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:56,780
Look at you.

274
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:58,180
You're getting along with them.

275
00:14:58,380 --> 00:14:58,680
Huh?

276
00:14:59,140 --> 00:14:59,960
That's great.

277
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:02,420
Getting along with them?

278
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:04,160
I was.

279
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,080
It's...

280
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:09,560
It's all thanks to you, Kaze Haya.

281
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:10,460
Huh?

282
00:15:10,460 --> 00:15:12,800
But I didn't do anything.

283
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:14,140
Yes, you did.

284
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:15,180
Kaze Haya,

285
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:18,340
you're the reason I was able to tell those two how I really felt.

286
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:21,440
I'm so glad I got to play the role of the ghost.

287
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,340
Know what, Kuro Numa?

288
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:25,980
You're actually really cheering.

289
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:28,680
And your attitude's so positive.

290
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:30,040
Cheery?

291
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:31,340
Me?

292
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:34,220
No one's told me that before.

293
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:36,460
Not in my entire life.

294
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,080
Stop staring.

295
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:42,940
I'm so sorry.

296
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:44,940
I let myself get carried away.

297
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:46,760
I promise I'll be extra careful.

298
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:48,560
Our eyes don't meet for over three seconds.

299
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:51,720
But I actually can't give you any bad luck so...

300
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:52,640
That isn't it.

301
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:54,500
That's embarrassing.

302
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,020
Don't make me say it.

303
00:15:57,020 --> 00:16:04,620
He stopped talking all of a sudden.

304
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:08,280
So, I don't know what I'm supposed to do anymore.

305
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,040
My heart's going crazy.

306
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:13,300
So many feelings I've never felt before.

307
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:16,400
It's almost like I've been reincarnated.

308
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:22,400
It seems like Kasehaya keeps giving me a lot of these firsts.

309
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:26,720
I'm truly grateful I got the chance to meet him.

310
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:29,240
We made it!

311
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,400
It's summer break!

312
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:33,600
Before we leave, I'll announce a test of courage results.

313
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:35,400
First things first, man.

314
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:37,060
You gotta accept your punishment.

315
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,240
You never managed to reach the goal.

316
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:41,120
Guess you found me out.

317
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:42,600
First place is Tonika.

318
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:44,300
The prize is 60 scrubbing brushes.

319
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:46,080
What am I supposed to do with that?

320
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:50,200
And next, the punishment for Kasehaya's last place is...

321
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:51,240
Wait for it!

322
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:55,700
For a whole entire week, you get to be Sanako's boyfriend!

323
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:58,440
What did he just say?

324
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:04,020
Kasehaya, so I heard you were together with Sanako last night.

325
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:06,320
Was she making a move on you?

326
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,820
Just get together already.

327
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:10,820
You guys are taking this way too far.

328
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:12,060
Yeah, no way.

329
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:13,740
I'll do anything but that.

330
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:16,540
Hey, that's kinda...

331
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:20,020
Calling that a punishment's just insanely rude.

332
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,440
Kuro Numa, she's a person.

333
00:17:22,940 --> 00:17:23,760
It's not funny.

334
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:26,600
Don't take that crap to heart.

335
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:27,400
Promise?

336
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:30,200
No.

337
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:33,100
You shouldn't defend me.

338
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:36,700
Kasehaya, your reputation...

339
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:37,740
You're gonna ruin it.

340
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:39,900
You've got it all wrong.

341
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:43,460
Well, not all of it.

342
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:45,840
It is true I was with Kasehaya yesterday.

343
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:47,280
But it...

344
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:47,900
It wasn't...

345
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,860
It really wasn't anything special, honestly.

346
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:54,280
It's just that...

347
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:57,560
Kasehaya is the type of person who treats everyone the same way.

348
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:00,000
I've got this.

349
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:01,780
It'll be okay.

350
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:04,220
I know how to clear up misunderstandings now.

351
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:06,400
That being said,

352
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:08,980
me being drawn to Kasehaya's kindness,

353
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:10,240
cheerfulness,

354
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:13,280
overwhelming positivity and honesty,

355
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,360
that's 100% fact.

356
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,280
So that part...

357
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,980
was not a misunderstanding.

358
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:28,260
Excuse me.

359
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:34,860
I'm sure I did the right thing.

360
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:40,420
That the misunderstanding was cleared up.

361
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:43,260
Since nothing I said was a lie,

362
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:46,040
every word of it was pure truth.

363
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:49,520
I'm sure I protected Kasehaya's reputation.

364
00:18:49,980 --> 00:18:52,060
I'm sure I did the right thing.

365
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:53,060
What?

366
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:55,100
Even though it's summer break?

367
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:55,940
Mm-hmm.

368
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:58,000
I promised to go help my teacher.

369
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:01,080
Yes.

370
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:02,740
I...

371
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:05,040
do believe I did the right thing.

372
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:06,420
Really.

373
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:13,120
But...

374
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:15,020
it sure does feel lonely.

375
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:18,220
One summer break is over.

376
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:20,640
I'm just so afraid that...

377
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:22,640
he...

378
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:24,760
he never looked me in the eyes ever again.

379
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:27,640
He may start avoiding me.

380
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:30,140
After all this time,

381
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:31,920
I thought I was used to it.

382
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:32,640
But...

383
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:34,540
the way he treated me

384
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:35,840
made me so happy

385
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:37,640
that I'd forgotten...

386
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:41,220
how my world felt

387
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:43,060
before I met Kasehaya.

388
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,480
He's making everything new.

389
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:51,960
Why?

390
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:54,520
It's summer break, so...

391
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:55,100
now what?

392
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:56,140
Here.

393
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:57,900
For the night's reel, MVP.

394
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,680
Everyone apologized.

395
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:06,740
I understood then.

396
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:08,260
It's cleared up.

397
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:09,440
Thank you

398
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:10,720
for defending me

399
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,440
and for going out of your way

400
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:13,340
to bring this here.

401
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,680
And you're still talking to me.

402
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,100
Thank you.

403
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:18,680
You know...

404
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:20,660
after hearing that,

405
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:22,260
I don't think you really

406
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:23,400
understand me that well.

407
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:25,580
Don't worry about me.

408
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:27,960
But I do know

409
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:29,360
how you feel, Kasehaya.

410
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:29,980
You don't!

411
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:35,800
It's...

412
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:37,640
okay to get my hopes up, right?

413
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:40,220
About being able to see you

414
00:20:40,220 --> 00:20:40,980
over summer break?

415
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:45,780
Back then?

416
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,080
Uh...

417
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,160
Um...

418
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:50,460
If you happen to be looking

419
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:51,580
for Kithohorohai,

420
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:53,100
it's that way.

421
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:55,820
Thanks a lot!

422
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,160
Mm-hmm.

423
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:04,080
The feeling that came over me

424
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:04,940
at that moment...

425
00:21:06,940 --> 00:21:08,020
Which has only continued

426
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:09,740
to grow and grow since then...

427
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:12,160
Someday...

428
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:15,100
Will it reach from me to you?

429
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:16,240
Thank you.

430
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:17,100
Oh, no.

431
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:18,980
Stop it empty.

432
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:22,360
They are ready and theyيلated by the day-long process.

433
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:24,300
You did?

434
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:32,240
Oh, no.

435
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:35,140
No, no.

436
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:37,280
The answer will be nothing.

437
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:41,280
シャボン玉飛ばそう

438
00:21:41,280 --> 00:21:46,280
空まではきっと届かない

439
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:49,280
家に壊れそう

440
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:54,280
未だら知りたいの永遠じゃない

441
00:21:54,280 --> 00:22:02,280
このままずっと見えていたいけど

442
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:07,280
その空いっぱいの神飛行機

443
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:11,280
ほらいにね

444
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:21,280
ひとつだけ見つけて

445
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:35,280
次回 シーティングチェンジ

446
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:06,280
気づきはいつど

447
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:11,280
はないね

448
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:13,280
Teresa

449
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:18,280
はないね

450
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:23,280
ゆおめん

